        "id": 10018,
        "name": "Edwin",
        "username": "Edwin",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/73ab20/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-30T22:11:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This came up in a game against the Vengeance Five this weekend; they were definitely losing so it didn't matter, but it occurred to me that as an insult added to injury, Hostage Situation reads as though it's completely impossible to get rid of (save with Bio-Engineering Beam if you happen to have that in play) if even one hero is incapacitated, since it specifically requires that \"each player\" discard a card, and the players of incapacitated heroes are still players but no longer have a hand, thusly discarding is impossible and the condition cannot be met, nor can they ever play cards to get rid of it while it's out.&nbsp; Has it been clarified that there is some exemption here, so that \"each player discards\" actually means \"each player who is capable of discarding chooses to do so and has at least one card in hand\"?</p><p>As an aside, does the goofy wording \"<strong>each </strong>player discards 1 card <strong>each</strong>\" signify something in relation to this question?&nbsp; Or has the wording been updated to fix this issue without my knowing (since I have a somewhat old printing of the Enhanced Edition, before the Ruling 15 revisions)?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:57.700Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
