        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>This came up in a game against the Vengeance Five this weekend; they were definitely losing so it didn&#39;t matter, but it occurred to me that as an insult added to injury, Hostage Situation reads as though it&#39;s completely impossible to get rid of (save with Bio-Engineering Beam if you happen to have that in play) if even one hero is incapacitated, since it specifically requires that &quot;each player&quot; discard a card, and the players of incapacitated heroes are still players but no longer have a hand, thusly discarding is impossible and the condition cannot be met, nor can they ever play cards to get rid of it while it&#39;s out.&nbsp; Has it been clarified that there is some exemption here, so that &quot;each player discards&quot; actually means &quot;each player who is capable of discarding chooses to do so and has at least one card in hand&quot;?</p><p>As an aside, does the goofy wording &quot;<strong>each </strong>player discards 1 card <strong>each</strong>&quot; signify something in relation to this question?&nbsp; Or has the wording been updated to fix this issue without my knowing (since I have a somewhat old printing of the Enhanced Edition, before the Ruling 15 revisions)?</p>",
