        "raw": "I&#39;ve always played these cards as though only [i]active[/i] heroes have to discard, since incapped ones don&#39;t have a deck. It&#39;s fine when only one card needs to be discarded but if you&#39;re in the Tomb of Anubis you can&#39;t ever get rid of the Trial of Fire if there&#39;s only one hero left because that needs H+2 cards with a maximum of three per player being discarded. We&#39;ve had that come up a couple of times, often in combination with the Swinging Blades when the surviving hero has soak (and that probably being the reason [i]why[/i] they&#39;ve survived ;)) so can&#39;t take the point of damage (we only ever have three heroes in the game so it is just a single point) to get rid of it. As a result, the environment ends up doing a lot of the work in damaging the villain since the surviving hero so far has been a card-saving Scholar or a Rhino-tanking Naturalist, neither of whom are in the best position to deal heaps of damage. But eventually, in their respective games, I think the Scholar was eventually able to Turn Loose while the Naturalist let the villain&#39;s hp get low enough and then went Croc and nommed &#39;em to death :D.\n",
